Sure! Here’s how you can print "Hello, World!" in some common programming languages:

### 1. Python
```python
print("Hello, World!")
```

### 2. JavaScript
```javascript
console.log("Hello, World!");
```

### 3. Java
```java
public class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");
    }
}
```

### 4. C++
```cpp
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::cout << "Hello, World!" << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

### 5. C#
```csharp
using System;

class Program {
    static void Main() {
        Console.WriteLine("Hello, World!");
    }
}
```

### 6. Ruby
```ruby
puts "Hello, World!"
```

### 7. PHP
```php
<?php
echo "Hello, World!";
?>
```

### 8. Swift
```swift
import Swift

print("Hello, World!")
```

### 9. Kotlin
```kotlin
fun main() {
    println("Hello, World!")
}
```

### 10. TypeScript
```typescript
console.log("Hello, World!");
```

Each of these examples will output "Hello, World!" when run. Choose the one that matches the language you are using or interested in.

